    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0430" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg334"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr.
                            White.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_apparent-typo-based-on-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 474.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch No. 419, of the
                    7th ultimo, with regard to the importation into Germany of American fruit waste
                    and the San Jose scale, I inclose for your information copy of a letter from the
                    Secretary of Agriculture stating that your request for exact information as to
                    the specific name of the insect referred to by the German authorities was a very
                    pertinent one, and that he would be pleased to learn the answer made by the
                    German Government.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
